SHELL

Run programs by name; they are searched in $PATH (/bin:/usr/bin:/home/bin:.).

  prog a "b c" 'd'     arguments, with quotes
  prog > file          write output to a file (>> appends)
  prog < file          read input from a file
  prog 2> file         write errors to a file
  a | b                a's output becomes b's input
  a ; b                run a, then b
  a && b               run b only if a succeeded (|| if it failed)
  prog &               run in the background (see ps, kill)
  $NAME ${NAME}        environment variables (set NAME=value)
  *.lua                file name patterns

Builtins: cd, pwd, set, unset, alias, unalias, exit.
Keys: Tab completes, Up/Down history, Ctrl+C stops the running
program, Ctrl+D on an empty line exits, Ctrl+Shift+V pastes.
